        "original_id": "ebaa410c-cba7-5c11-83b0-5863b613be2c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Danny Bonaduce, Joseph Bonaduce, Bonnie Franklin, Mackenzie Phillips, Valerie Bertinelli, Cheyenne Haynes\n- Roles: radio/television personality, comedian, professional wrestler, child actor, TV writer, producer, host, judge\n- TV Shows: One Day at a Time, I Know My Kid's a Star, The Partridge Family, The Dick Van Dyke Show\n- Films: Lies in Plain Sight\n- Organizations: CBS, Lifetime Movie Network\n- Places: Broomall, Pennsylvania, Indianapolis\n\nFacts:\n- One Day at a Time is an American sitcom that aired on CBS from December 16, 1975, until May 28, 1984.\n- One Day at a Time starred Bonnie Franklin as a divorced mother raising two teenage daughters in Indianapolis, and Mackenzie Phillips and Valerie Bertinelli played the daughters.\n- Danny Bonaduce was born on August 13, 1959, in Broomall, Pennsylvania.\n- Danny Bonaduce is an American radio and television personality, comedian, professional wrestler, and former child actor.\n- Danny Bonaduce is the son of veteran TV writer and producer Joseph Bonaduce, who worked on The Dick Van Dyke Show and One Day at a Time.\n- Danny Bonaduce was known as a child actor on the 1970s TV show The Partridge Family.\n- Danny Bonaduce is the host and primary judge of I Know My Kid's a Star.\n- Cheyenne Haynes appeared in the Lifetime Movie Network television film Lies in Plain Sight and in I Know My Kid's a Star.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "d1edbe1b-b1e7-512a-b032-94356df603bf",
        "text": "Page: Danny Bonaduce. Sentence: Dante Daniel \"Danny\" Bonaduce (born August 13, 1959) is an American radio/television personality, comedian, professional wrestler, and former child actor.\nPage: Danny Bonaduce. Sentence: Born in Broomall, Pennsylvania, Bonaduce is the son of veteran TV writer/producer Joseph Bonaduce (\"The Dick Van Dyke Show\", \"One Day at a Time\", etc.).\nPage: One Day at a Time. Sentence: One Day at a Time is an American sitcom that aired on CBS from December 16, 1975, until May 28, 1984.\nPage: One Day at a Time. Sentence: It starred Bonnie Franklin as a divorced mother raising two teenage daughters, played by Mackenzie Phillips and Valerie Bertinelli, in Indianapolis.\nPage: I Know My Kid's a Star. Sentence: The show's host and primary judge is Danny Bonaduce, who is best known as having been a child actor himself on the 1970s TV show \"The Partridge Family\".\nPage: Cheyenne Haynes. Sentence: Her notable works include the Lifetime Movie Network television film, \"Lies in Plain Sight\", and \"I Know My Kid's a Star\".",
